$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure - A mixture of ketoxime ,
and anhydrous AlCl3 was throughly ground in an agate motor for a few
minutes. Hydrogen chloride was evolved violently. The molten mass was
ground by heating (40-80°C) for 30 min. The reaction mixture was mixed
with crushed-ice and extracted with CHCl3. The chloroform solution was
dried over MgSO4. The solvent was removed in vaccuo to give the product.
Table 1. Entry 6, yield 100%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A facile Beckmann rearrangement of oximes with AlCl3 in the solid state
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ghiaci, M.; Imanzadeh, G. Hassan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (1998), 28(12), 2275-2280

