$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure for the Reaction of 1a (Table 1, entry 8): A mixture of
TAPC (0.01 mmol, 3.5 mg) and HFIP (2 mL) was placed in a 20 mL
round-bottomed flask, and 1a (1 mmol, 197 mg) was added to the flask.
Then the mixture was stirred at 70 ºC for 2 h. After removal of the
solvent under reduced pressure, 2a (190 mg) was isolated by column
chromatography on silica gel (n-hexane/ethyl acetate ) 1/1) in 96% yield.
