$DATUM 75-05-8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure. A solution of ketoxime (1
mmol), 10 % mol PPh3 and 10 % mol I2 in MeCN was refluxed for determinate
time. After completion of the reaction as monitored by TLC, the reaction
was stopped and cooled to room temperature, concentrated in vacuo. The
residue was dissolved in EtOAc and washed with saturated sodium
thiosulfate solution. The organic layer was separated, washed with NaCl
saturated aqueous, then concentrated. The resulting crude product was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel to give the corresponding
amide. N-p-methoxyphenylacemide (2b), Yield: 96 %, time: 10 min. m.p.
128-130 °C; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): 8.20 (br s, 1H), 7.60 (d, J=7.7 Hz,
2H), 6.83 (d, J=8.6 Hz, 2H), 3.78 (s, 3H), 2.20 (s, 3H); UHR-MS (ESI):
m/z calc. for C9H11NO2+[Na] 188.0687, found 188.0675 (M+ +Na).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Beckmann rearrangement, mechanism studied
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ph3P/I2-catalyzed Beckmann rearrangement of ketoximes into amides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Xu, Feng; Wang, Ni-Ge; Tian, You-Ping; Chen, Yong-Mei; Liu, Wei-Chun
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2012), 42(23), 3532-3539

