$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for the Preparation of
Amides.- bis-(Trichloromethyl) carbonate (0.30 g, 1 mmol) was dissolved
in 2 mL MeCN, cooled in ice bath for 20 min, then DMF (0.25 mL, 3 mmol)
was added dropwise to the mixture, stirred in the ice bath for 1 hour.
Then the ketoxime (3 mmol) was added in one portion and the mixture was
heated to reflux for the time given in Table 2. After completion of the
reaction as monitored by TLC, the reaction was quenched with saturated
aqueous NaHCO3 (10 mL) and the product was extracted with ethyl acetate
(10 mL x 3). The combined organic layer washed with water (10 mL), dried
over anhydrous sodium sulfate, and concentrated under reduced pressure.
The crude product was purified by column chromatography using a mixture
of petroleum ether/ ethyl acetate (v:v = 8:1) as the eluent. Entry: 3c,
Yield: 95%. mp.: 124.0-125.1 °C, lit. mp.: 13010a °C. MS (CI+) m/z: 165
(M+), IR cm-1: 3243 1648 1605, 1H NMR (δ): 7.61 (s, 1 H, NH), 7.38 (d, 2
H, J = 8.8 Hz, ArH), 6.83 (d, 2 H , J = 8.8 Hz, ArH), 3.78 (s, 3 H,
OCH3), 2.13 (s, 3 H, CH3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, mechanism studied, Beckmann rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A simple and efficient procedure for the Beckmann rearrangement of oxime
using bis(trichloromethyl) carbonate/DMF
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Su, W. K.; Zhang, Y.; Li, J. J.; Li, P.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Preparations and Procedures International (2008), 40(6), 543-550

