$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Montmorillonite K 10 was dried and simultaneously activated in a
microwave oven for 3 min at 780 W prior to use. In a typical experiment,
the oxime (300 mg) was intimately mixed with clay and the glass vessel
(Pyrex) was irradiated in a domestic microwave oven during the
appropriated time at 780 W; after cooling, the reaction mixture is washed
with diethyl ether followed by filtration of clay and removal of the
solvent under reduced pressure and the products were isolated and
purified by crystallization. All amides and lactams prepared are known
compounds identified by physical properties (m.p., IR and 1H-RMN) and
compared with those of authentic samples. 1a, yield 95%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM montmorillonite K10 catalyst; microwaves
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave assisted Beckman rearrangement of ketoximes in dry media
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
