$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Beckmann Rearrangement A
solution of a ketoxime (1 mmol) and catalytic amount of H2SO4 (0.5 mmol)
in an ionic liquid (1 mL) was placed in a flat bottom flask and mixed
thoroughly on a vortex mixer (Scientific Inc., Model G-560). The mixture
was irradiated intermittently in an unmodified domestic microwave oven
for 60 s (20 + 20 + 20 s), and loaded on silica column chromatography
directly to isolate product. Table 2 entry 5, yield 99%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, ionic liq.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Thermal behaviors of ionic liquids under microwave irradiation and their
application on microwave-assisted catalytic Beckmann rearrangement of
ketoximes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lee, Jae Kyun; Kim, Dok-Chan; Song, Choong Eui; Lee, Sang-gi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2003), 33(13), 2301-2307

