$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Beckmann Rearrangement (General Procedure) : A
mixture of the ketoximes (0.4g) and FeCl3- Mont K10 (1 g) (or any other
clay as is specified in Table 1) was stirred in toluene at its reflux
temperature. The reaction was monitored by TLC. The mixture was cooled
and filtered. The clay residue was extracted with boiling acetone and the
extract was combined with the toluene filterate. The solvent was vacuum
distilled to yield the anilide which was recrystallized from a suitable
solvent or purified by column chromatography (Ethyl Acetate - Hexane).
Table 2 Entry 4, yield 97%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Beckmann rearrangement of substituted diaryl ketoximes using FeCl3
impregnated montmorillonite K10
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pai, S. G.; Bajpai, A. R.; Deshpande, A. B.; Samant, S. D.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (1997), 27(3), 379-384

